  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Key Takeaway:</strong> The equivalence principle—that gravity and acceleration are locally
    indistinguishable—is the foundation of general relativity. This deceptively simple idea explains why inertial
    and gravitational mass are equal, predicts gravitational effects on light, and led Einstein to understand
    gravity as spacetime curvature. It remains one of the most precisely tested principles in all of physics.
  </p>
